{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And Miriam the prophetess took.</b> Where was she prophesied? When she was the sister of Aharon — before Moshe was born — she said: my mother is destined to bear a son, etc., as is in Sotah (12b). Another interpretation: 'sister of Aharon' — because he risked his life for her when she was stricken with tzara'at, she is called by his name." "<b>The timbrel.</b> An instrument of the musical kind." "<b>With timbrels and with dances.</b> The righteous women of that generation were confident that the Holy One, blessed be He, would perform miracles for them, so they brought timbrels out of Egypt (Mekhilta)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:52:30.838913157Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}